# ---- Python ----
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---- Logs & scratch ----
*.log
*.out

# ---- Internal working docs (not for the public release / reviewers) ----
REVIEWER_RESPONSE_PLAN.md
# The adversarial-review record: per-persona finding files, severity triage, decision log.
# Useful to the author, and to nobody else -- a public "hostile-competitor.json" and a
# HIGH_SEVERITY.md are read as a list of the paper's weak points, not as diligence.
audit_recovered/
# Correspondence with a journal. It has no reproducibility function, and the manuscripts
# published from this work point reviewers at this repository: a cover letter addressed to
# one journal's editor, and a point-by-point response to that journal's reviewers, are
# handed to the next editor by the data-availability statement. Kept on disk, off the
# remote. Anything the reader needs is in the manuscript.
paper/cover_letter.*
paper/response_to_reviewers.*
# Backups and partial runs. A ".bak" beside a results CSV is ambiguous to a replicator in
# exactly the way the paper warns about, and a partial file is not a result.
*.csv.bak
*_partial_backup.csv
# The venue packages. These name three target journals, rank them, and state which
# submission is live where. The data-availability statement in every manuscript points a
# reviewer at this repository, so anything left tracked here is handed to the editor of
# whichever venue is being submitted to -- including the fact that two rival packages are
# built and waiting. Untracked is not enough on its own: `git add -A` would take them.
submissions/
# exploratory from-scratch transformer; underfits short DNA, not used in the paper
exp_transformer.py
pg-*.png
*.synctex.gz

# ---- Cloned OUP template source + bundled zips (not ours to redistribute) ----
template_src/

# ---- Genomic Benchmarks RAW SEQUENCE DATA -- NOT redistributed here ----
# (downloaded on demand via the genomic-benchmarks package; cached outside this tree)
.genomic_benchmarks/
# on-disk pickle/npy cache of the sequence data (built by prefetch.py)
datacache/
